\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.3}{\ignorespaces The Strain Sensitivity of the aLIGO and A+ detectors. The noise due to radiation pressure and photon shot noise is shown in dark-blue (aLIGO) and dark-red (A+). Above 10\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz, quantum effects are one of the limiting sources of noise; with the other being the noise due to Brownian motion of the mirror's coating. Below 10\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz, seismic noise begins to dominate the noise of the detector.\relax }}{26}{figure.caption.32}}
\newlabel{fig:detectorchapterdesignsensitivitycurves}{{1.3}{26}{The Strain Sensitivity of the aLIGO and A+ detectors. The noise due to radiation pressure and photon shot noise is shown in dark-blue (aLIGO) and dark-red (A+). Above 10\,Hz, quantum effects are one of the limiting sources of noise; with the other being the noise due to Brownian motion of the mirror's coating. Below 10\,Hz, seismic noise begins to dominate the noise of the detector.\relax }{figure.caption.32}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.4}{\ignorespaces Sketch of a LIGO detector. The input and output optics, IM1-4, input periscope, OM1-3, OMC, IFI and OFI, are shown in blue. The input mode cleaner is shown in green. The power recycling is shown in pink. The arm cavities are shown in pale blue. The signal recycling cavity is shown in yellow.\relax }}{27}{figure.caption.33}}
\newlabel{fig:ligolayout}{{1.4}{27}{Sketch of a LIGO detector. The input and output optics, IM1-4, input periscope, OM1-3, OMC, IFI and OFI, are shown in blue. The input mode cleaner is shown in green. The power recycling is shown in pink. The arm cavities are shown in pale blue. The signal recycling cavity is shown in yellow.\relax }{figure.caption.33}{}}
